3. UNDERLYING PUBLIC-RECORD SOURCES
-----------------------------------

The repository archives or references material drawn from the following
public-record sources. These sources are NOT owned, licensed, or
sublicensable by the maintainers of this repository. Use of the source
material itself is governed by the policies of the originating
agencies and copyright holders, and is generally permitted as public
record under Texas and federal law:

  * Parker County Appraisal District — appraisal notices, certified roll,
    parcel data (Texas Tax Code, Texas Public Information Act).
  * Texas Commission on Environmental Quality — Central Registry, air
    permit registrations, regulated-entity records (statutorily public).
  * Texas Comptroller of Public Accounts — franchise tax registry,
    Chapter 312 / 313 / JETI registries (statutorily public).
  * Texas Water Development Board — groundwater conservation district
    shapefile (public domain).
  * USDA National Agricultural Statistics Service — Census of
    Agriculture 2022 (public domain US Government work).
  * Parker County Commissioners Court — public meeting recordings and
    transcripts (Texas Open Meetings Act).

The CC-BY-4.0 license above applies to our compilation, analysis, and
presentation of this material. The original source records remain
subject to their own terms.


